# ── Optional override ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set VITE_API_BASE_URL ONLY when you intentionally want the frontend to call
# Django directly instead of going through Vite's /api proxy. In normal dev
# (same machine), the proxy is strictly better and this should be blank.
# Typical use case: running the SPA on a different host while the API lives at
# a published URL during dev.  For production builds use `vite build` with
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-host.example.com/  npm run build
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/api
